🚽 Test case: #196 -- a pointer-typed struct/union VARIABLE used as the
🚽 base of member access follows the pointer for a plain SCALAR field
🚽 (not just an array field, which struct_pointer_array_field.brainrot
🚽 already covers) -- PR #248 review, finding 4: the original test set
🚽 only exercised the array-field shape. Also covers assignment-after-
🚽 declaration (`pp = &f;` as a separate statement, not folded into the
🚽 declarator) and write-through visibility from the original variable.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Point p;
    p.x = 1;
    p.y = 2;

    gang Point *pp;
    pp = &p;
    pp.x = 42;

    yapping("%d %d %d", pp.x, pp.y, p.x);
}
